  "review": {
    "main_split": "The exact Entrypoint.main_source theorem type and rfl body move to EntrypointExecutableProofs; generic EntrypointProofs no longer imports HostMain. This permits controller/host ordinary composition without a Main symbol collision.",
    "native_fixture": "Two real Linux renames in fresh owned directories. Each creates an independent peer at the old staging name; one returns synthetic EIO and the other loses its ACK. The actual finishCommit source preserves both committed bytes and peer bytes. This does not exercise a network filesystem or add a production fault switch.",
    "publication": "All rename acknowledgements close the three actual owned raw descriptors only. No native errno is assumed to exclude a commit. Pre-attempt cleanup and public storage-failure/report projection are preserved. Error/lost source witnesses are constructive.",
    "validator": "Only an actual successful wait status produces reaped=true. Both successful validation and policy rejection may clean up; unknown spawn/wait releases raw handles while retaining backing names/files. stdout EOF and error text never produce reaping. Every unknown-finish source prefix has only its two owned close requests.",
    "vm": "Existing ReadSafe public theorem headers are unchanged, but BoundedEffect is deliberately strengthened to include engine-side namespace passivity. One source traversal is generalized to SourceProfile with exact spawn arguments, covering every reply/loss. No backend child-lifetime or whole-VM filesystem frame follows. This is a reviewed extension of host-vm-review, not a silent replacement of its scope."
  },
